{title: Let the Lower Lights Be Burning}
{artist: Philip P. Bliss}
{genre: Gospel}
{style: Traditional}
{flow: Closing}
{key: A}
{key_original: Bb}
{tempo: 95}
{time: 3/4}
{c: Chords checked against the four-part harmony of the Cyber Hymnal score (Tabernacle Hymns Number Five (Chicago, Illinois: Tabernacle Publishing, 1955), # 60)}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[A]Brightly beams our Father’s [D]mercy
[D]From His [B7]lighthouse ever[E7]more,
[A]But to us He gives the [D]keeping
[D]Of the [A]lights along the shore.
[A]Let the [D]lower lights be [A]burning!
[A]Send a [B]gleam across the [E7]wave!
[A]For to us He gives the [D]keeping
[D]Of the [A]lights along the shore.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[A]Dark the night of sin has [D]settled,
[D]Loud the [B7]angry billows [E7]roar;
[A]Eager eyes are watching, [D]longing
[D]For the [A]lights along the shore.
[A]Let the [D]lower lights be [A]burning!
[A]Send a [B]gleam across the [E7]wave!
[A]Eager eyes are watching, [D]longing
[D]For the [A]lights along the shore.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[A]Trim your feeble lamp, my [D]brother,
[D]Some poor [B7]sailor tempest [E7]tossed,
[A]Trying now to make the [D]harbor,
[D]In the [A]darkness may be lost.
[A]Let the [D]lower lights be [A]burning!
[A]Send a [B]gleam across the [E7]wave!
[A]Trying now to make the [D]harbor,
[D]Some poor [A]sailor may be lost.
{end_of_verse}
